{
  "id": "sphingomyelin-lipidosis",
  "term": "sphingomyelin lipidosis",
  "definition": "Sphingomyelin lipidosis is the classic infantile form of Niemann-Pick disease caused by a mutation affecting sphingomyelin phosphodiesterase. It involves buildup of sphingomyelins in immune-system scavenger cells and other body cells, leading to cell death and problems such as jaundice, enlarged liver and spleen, and severe brain damage.",
